  "worked_solution": "We recall the graph of $y={(\\frac{1}{3})}^{x}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14258364/assets/81be7f2983aeb647a8fa88e2caad8cea3c2052190222670838077e760a2e7fda.png)\n\nFrom the graph, we see that the function increases without bound as $x$ decreases.  Therefore,\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }{(\\frac{1}{3})}^{x}=\\infty .\n$$",
